    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d691">

                <pb facs="1073" n="977" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg977"/>

                <head>No. 689.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Admiral Polo de
                    Bernabé.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-11-12"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 12,
                        1873</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Admiral</hi> This Department has received a telegram
                    from an official source, representing that the captain of the Virginius, so
                    called, thirty-six of the crew, and sixteen other persons, were shot on the 7th
                    and 8th instants. This information relates to an act apparently too shocking and
                    cruel to be credible. I am in hopes that more authentic intelligence may have
                    reached you, which would tend to discredit the statement referred to. I will
                    consequently thank you to relieve, as soon as you conveniently can, our natural
                    anxiety upon the subject.</p>
                <p>I avail, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
